      "urpx:forRatePlan": {
        "@id": "gpc:tc-u"
      },
      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "gpc:cc-tc-u-2026-06-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "gpc:cc-tc-u-2026-06-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 7 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Devices counts. Each device charge is priced per device of one kind. URPX v0.5.1 names no profile property for a count of devices of a kind, so each device's MetricInput is a urpx:profileMetricInput that names no urpx:profileMetricProperty and states the kind in its name, in the pattern of Jackson EMC's Schedule S-26; a consumer supplies the counts. (2) Fuel seasons by billing month. FCR-27 prices June through September and October through May, which Schedule R's bills show is read by the billing month a bill is rendered in. The JSON-LD gates the fuel PriceDefinitions on calendar months, so usage in the weeks a billing period runs ahead of its billing month takes the other season's fuel price. (3) Fuel Cost Recovery voltage levels. FCR-27 also prices Primary Distribution and Transmission customers. Only the Secondary Distribution rates are carried, as Prices with no condition, so they apply to every customer on the schedule. (4) Municipal Franchise Fee base. MFF-11 applies to the total revenues of each bill, which include the ECCR-15 and DSM-C-15 amounts. Its multiplier Prices here are based on each device charge's Price and on the fuel subtotal, not on the ECCR and DSM-C multiplier Prices, so the franchise fee on those two amounts, about 0.44 percent of the base bill inside city limits, is not carried. (5) Unmetered energy. The sheet bills each device by its demand, in 60-watt increments, and applies Fuel Cost Recovery to the bill, but states no monthly kWh for a device. FCR-27 is carried per kWh on a kWh MetricInput the consumer supplies; how the Company estimates an unmetered device's kWh is not stated and not carried. (6) Device and increment counts. The Basic Service Charge is per device, including its first 60 watts of demand, and each further 60 watts is priced per increment, so a consumer counts each device's watts above 60 in whole increments; how a part increment is counted is not stated. (7) Term of Contract. One year. Nothing is priced by it and it is not carried.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-19T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
